> I thought of making this thread first off because I had a +4 r'of
> increase accuracy and a +3 of increase damage and wanted to know which
> was better, but I think an open ended question might be more fun:
> 
> What are your personal best ring choices, ignoring any which give
> intrinsics that can be gotten by other means? What do you use in your
> ascention kit?
> 
> Also, what's better, increase damage or increase accuracy?Or
> protection?

Forget the ring of protection; it's useful at most in the very early
game. Increase damage is nice if it's either well charged or if you
have a free ring slot anyway. Most valuable is conflict. Valuable,
but with slightly decreasing value from early to late game, is a
ring of regeneration. Helpful in certain situations is levitation.
Searching and warning are both helpful throughout the whole game.
Free action is very good to prevent effects from thrown paralysis
potions. If you lack intrinsic teleport control use the ring.

What I seem to have mostly worn during ascensions are rings of free
action, regeneration, and increase damage. In my bag are very often
conflict, levitation, and most of the other useful rings mentioned
above.

